{"title":"Theil index calculator","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Theil index calculator","subtitle":"Compute Theil indices, their decomposition, bias and standard errors with your own data","toc":false,"html-table-processing":"none"},"headingText":"How to interpret the results","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nPaste your data or upload a CSV file to obtain the Theil indices $T_0$ (mean log deviation) and $T_1$, their **jackknife bias** and **standard error**, a **bias-corrected estimate with a 95% confidence interval**, and, if you choose a grouping variable, the **decomposition into between-group and within-group inequality**.\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\n**Your data never leave your computer.** All calculations run in your browser; nothing is uploaded or stored. The jackknife is computed in $\\mathcal{O}(n)$ with the closed-form expressions of THEILUMINA's preliminary results, so it is instantaneous even with hundreds of thousands of observations.\n:::\n\n```{=html}\n<script src=\"js/theil-calc.js\"></script>\n<div class=\"calc\">\n  <div class=\"calc-step\">\n    <h3>1. Your data</h3>\n    <p>Paste a list of incomes (one per line, or separated by spaces or semicolons), <b>or</b> a table with a header row (CSV, semicolon- or tab-separated, e.g. copied from Excel), <b>or</b> upload a file.</p>\n    <textarea id=\"calc-input\" class=\"form-control\" rows=\"9\" placeholder=\"income;sex&#10;12;Woman&#10;16;Man&#10;...\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"calc-row\">\n      <input id=\"calc-file\" type=\"file\" accept=\".csv,.txt,.tsv\" class=\"form-control\" aria-label=\"Upload a CSV file\">\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"list\">Example: list of incomes</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"sex\">Example: incomes by sex</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"regions\">Example: 2,000 simulated incomes in 4 regions</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"calc-step\" id=\"calc-cols\" hidden>\n    <h3>2. Variables</h3>\n    <div class=\"calc-row\">\n      <label>Income variable <select id=\"calc-y\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n      <label>Groups (optional) <select id=\"calc-g\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n      <label>Sampling weights (optional) <select id=\"calc-w\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"calc-row\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"calc-run\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Compute</button></div>\n  <div id=\"calc-msg\"></div>\n  <div id=\"calc-out\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<script src=\"js/calculator-ui.js\"></script>\n```\n\n\n- **Estimate:** the usual (plug-in) estimator of each index.\n- **Jackknife bias:** estimated bias of that estimator. Theil estimators are usually **biased downwards**, especially in small samples and with heavy-tailed distributions.\n- **Bias-corrected estimate:** estimate minus the jackknife bias.\n- **Standard error and 95% interval:** precision of the estimate. Differences between groups, regions or years should be interpreted in the light of these margins of error.\n\nThe **theil** R package, under development in THEILUMINA, will provide these and more accurate methods (bias prediction, improved confidence intervals and complex survey designs).\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nPaste your data or upload a CSV file to obtain the Theil indices $T_0$ (mean log deviation) and $T_1$, their **jackknife bias** and **standard error**, a **bias-corrected estimate with a 95% confidence interval**, and, if you choose a grouping variable, the **decomposition into between-group and within-group inequality**.\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\n**Your data never leave your computer.** All calculations run in your browser; nothing is uploaded or stored. The jackknife is computed in $\\mathcal{O}(n)$ with the closed-form expressions of THEILUMINA's preliminary results, so it is instantaneous even with hundreds of thousands of observations.\n:::\n\n```{=html}\n<script src=\"js/theil-calc.js\"></script>\n<div class=\"calc\">\n  <div class=\"calc-step\">\n    <h3>1. Your data</h3>\n    <p>Paste a list of incomes (one per line, or separated by spaces or semicolons), <b>or</b> a table with a header row (CSV, semicolon- or tab-separated, e.g. copied from Excel), <b>or</b> upload a file.</p>\n    <textarea id=\"calc-input\" class=\"form-control\" rows=\"9\" placeholder=\"income;sex&#10;12;Woman&#10;16;Man&#10;...\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"calc-row\">\n      <input id=\"calc-file\" type=\"file\" accept=\".csv,.txt,.tsv\" class=\"form-control\" aria-label=\"Upload a CSV file\">\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"list\">Example: list of incomes</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"sex\">Example: incomes by sex</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm\" data-example=\"regions\">Example: 2,000 simulated incomes in 4 regions</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"calc-step\" id=\"calc-cols\" hidden>\n    <h3>2. Variables</h3>\n    <div class=\"calc-row\">\n      <label>Income variable <select id=\"calc-y\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n      <label>Groups (optional) <select id=\"calc-g\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n      <label>Sampling weights (optional) <select id=\"calc-w\" class=\"form-select\"></select></label>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"calc-row\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"calc-run\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Compute</button></div>\n  <div id=\"calc-msg\"></div>\n  <div id=\"calc-out\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<script src=\"js/calculator-ui.js\"></script>\n```\n\n## How to interpret the results\n\n- **Estimate:** the usual (plug-in) estimator of each index.\n- **Jackknife bias:** estimated bias of that estimator. Theil estimators are usually **biased downwards**, especially in small samples and with heavy-tailed distributions.\n- **Bias-corrected estimate:** estimate minus the jackknife bias.\n- **Standard error and 95% interval:** precision of the estimate. Differences between groups, regions or years should be interpreted in the light of these margins of error.\n\nThe **theil** R package, under development in THEILUMINA, will provide these and more accurate methods (bias prediction, improved confidence intervals and complex survey designs).\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":true,"code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":true,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true,"html-table-processing":"none"},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","toc":false,"toc-depth":2,"html-math-method":"katex","include-after-body":["_goatcounte